content.text:
The `search` service is the one root cause. Its outgoing calls to `rate` are held back for about 2.5 s before they reach `rate`, and that delay reaches users through `frontend`'s `/hotels` path.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT c.service_name cli, s.service_name srv, c.span_name, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(c.duration,0.5)/1e6,1) cli_p50_ms, round(approx_quantile(s.duration,0.5)/1e6,2) srv_p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id AND s.trace_id = c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND s.service_name='rate' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "search→rate GetRates client spans take about 2.7 s at p95, while rate's server spans stay near 1 ms."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT c.service_name cli, s.service_name srv, c.duration/1e6 cdur_ms, s.duration/1e6 sdur_ms, (epoch(s.time)-epoch(c.time))*1000 AS srv_start_off_ms, (epoch(c.time)+c.duration/1e9 - epoch(s.time)-s.duration/1e9)*1000 AS end_gap_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id AND s.trace_id = c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND s.service_name='rate' ORDER BY c.duration DESC LIMIT 12", "claim": "Rate's server span starts about 2.5 s after search's client span starts, so the delay is before the request reaches rate."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT c.service_name cli, s.service_name srv, c.span_name, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(c.duration,0.5)/1e6,2) cli_p50_ms, round(approx_quantile(s.duration,0.5)/1e6,2) srv_p50_ms FROM normal_traces c JOIN normal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id AND s.trace_id = c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND s.service_name='rate' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "In the normal period, search→rate GetRates client spans take roughly 9 ms at median."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT c.service_name cli, s.service_name srv, c.span_name, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(c.duration,0.5)/1e6,2) cli_p50_ms, round(approx_quantile(s.duration,0.5)/1e6,2) srv_p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id AND s.trace_id = c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND s.service_name='geo' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "search→geo calls stay fast in the incident (about 0.4 ms), so the fault is specific to the rate path."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT 'abn' s, service_name, metric, round(avg(value),3) av FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='search' AND metric IN ('k8s.pod.cpu.usage','k8s.pod.memory.working_set') GROUP BY 2,3 UNION ALL SELECT 'nor', service_name, metric, round(avg(value),3) FROM normal_metrics WHERE service_name='search' AND metric IN ('k8s.pod.cpu.usage','k8s.pod.memory.working_set') GROUP BY 2,3", "claim": "Search pod CPU and memory are unchanged from normal, so search is not resource-saturated."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [
      {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT c.service_name cli, s.service_name srv, c.span_name, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(c.duration,0.5)/1e6,1) cli_p50_ms, round(approx_quantile(s.duration,0.5)/1e6,2) srv_p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id AND s.trace_id = c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='frontend' AND s.service_name='search' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "frontend's search.Search/Nearby calls to search take about 1.8 s at median, matching search's server time."}
    ]}
  ]
}
```

